Figure~\ref{overview} illustrates the overall workflow of \toolname{}, which consists of four stages.
In the patch selection stage, a partial patch is selected from the patch tree with the goal of refining it into a plausible candidate.
In the patch generation stage, new patches are generated based on the selected partial patch, leveraging Chain-of-Thought (CoT) reasoning and self-reflection techniques to enhance the quality of generated patches.
