\circlednumber{2} The Huffman coding~\cite{huffman1952method} algorithm is an entropy-based method that assigns a shorter codeword to more frequent symbols. Data transformation does not affect entropy. Therefore, data transformation without decomposing byte clusters does not affect the compression ratio of Huffman codes.
