\vspace{-2mm}\section{Conclusion}\label{se:conclusion}
We proposed a CSI-free detection framework for atomic MU-MIMO receivers using ICL. ICL eliminates explicit channel estimation by directly mapping pilot-response examples and received symbols to transmitted symbols. Simulation shows that ICL achieves higher accuracy and lower latency compared to state-of-the-art optimization-based approaches across various settings. The findings support the use of AI-native detection for scalable and real-time atomic receivers.

