\title{Kuratowski Monoids on Posets}
\author{Mark Bowron}

\maketitle

\begin{abstract}\noindent
Gardner and Jackson \cite{2008_gardner_jackson} proved that six different \textit{Kuratowski monoids\/}
(generated by complement and topological closure under composition) occur in nonempty spaces.  
Many analogues have appeared since
(see the references).\vphantom{\cite{2012_al-hassani_mahesar_coen_sorge_a}
\cite{2018_banakh_chervak_martynyuk_pylypovych_ravsky_simkiv}
\cite{2024_bowron} \cite{2011_brzozowski_grant_shallit} \cite{2014_brzozowski_jiraskova_zou}
\cite{2021_canilang_cohen_graese_seong} \cite{2023_caron_durand_patrou} \cite{2012_cato}
\cite{2013_charlier_domaratzki_harju_shallit} \cite{2025_ciraulo}
\cite{2020_cohen_johnson_kral_li_soll} \cite{2019_dassow} \cite{2018_farajzadeh_shafie} \cite{2008_gardner_jackson}
\cite{2017_gupta_sarma} \cite{2017_jirasek_palmovsky_sebej} \cite{2016_jirasek_sebej} \cite{2019_santiago}
\cite{2017_schwiebert} \cite{2011_shallit_willard} \cite{2010_sherman} \cite{2017_shum}}
We use some recent results of Ciraulo \cite{2025_ciraulo} to prove:

\medskip\noindent
$1.$ Operators $c,i$ on an arbitrary poset
subject to the usual general closure and interior axioms---but not subject to the usual duality, for there
is no complement---always generate one of $18$ different monoids.

\medskip\noindent
$2.$ No edges are missing in the interior-pseudocomplement Hasse diagram in \cite{2025_ciraulo} (p.\,$21$).

\medskip\noindent
\emph{Keywords}: closure, interior, pseudocomplement, Kuratowski monoid, poset.

\medskip\noindent
\emph{MSC}: 54A05 (primary), 06F05 (secondary)

\end{abstract}

