Figure~\ref{fig:figS6}(a-e) shows the temperature dependence of $S$ at fixed applied magnetic fields for all samples. Below $\sim 25 \mathrm{\ K}$, $S$ is smaller at higher magnetic fields, whereas above it, lower fields result in smaller values of $S$.  Lastly, Fig.~\ref{fig:figS7}(a-e) is the energy scale $U^*/k_B = T / S$ versus $1/J$ used to extract the exponent $\mu$. The exact fit range used is in Table \ref{tab:samples1}.



