Monitoring features, such as human fatigue levels, necessitate the collection of sensitive data, like heart rate. 
In line with our ethical considerations (cf. RO-2), \emph{we will develop methods that enable effective human monitoring while preserving privacy}. This will involve incorporating our human-value complemented design strategies into CPS, starting from the requirements engineering process to find a balance between system requirements and privacy concerns.
